  "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A\u21d4B$ is true if $A\u21d2B$ **and** $B\u21d2A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A\u21d4B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nFirst, we add a column for $\u00acP:$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,R\\,$ | $\\,\u00acP\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $\u00acP\u21d4R.$ \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,R\\,$ | $\\,\u00acP\\,$ | $\\,\u00acP\u21d4R\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |",
